    "stdout": "Meridian Credits release 1.0 credit agreement (approved by Finance, see trial-4mw): Each charge line's uncapped credit is 10% of charge_cents, rounded down separately to integer cents (floor(charge_cents*10/100)). The 2400-cent credit cap is shared by all lines with the same (account_id, subscription_id) pair; distinct (account_id, subscription_id) pairs have independent caps. Within a cap group, credit is assigned to lines in priority order: earliest service_on first, ties broken by increasing line_id (Unicode code-point order). Each line receives its uncapped credit up to the group's remaining cap; later lines in priority order receive only the remaining credit, or zero once exhausted. Total credit = sum of assigned line credits; a line's amount_due_cents = charge_cents - assigned credit; total due = total charges - total credit. A one-line quote (command=quote) treats the supplied line as the entire statement/cap group, so its credit is simply min(floor(charge_cents*0.1), 2400). Release is versioned: an omitted release selects the current agreement; \"1.0\" is the initial agreement and remains supported after later releases are introduced.\n",
    "stderr": "",
    "stdout_base64": "",
    "stderr_base64": ""
